(:spec :id conductorConfig :v 1 :date "2026-10-30" :file "<conductor store>/ladder.asn" :reader "asl/tools/coord/conductor.asl pfCfg rungCap" :check "asl/tools/coord/conductor.asl pfErrors (tested in conductorTest testProviderFail)"
  :doc "per-store escalation settings of the conductor, one row per line; the store is the --store directory of the conductor (~/.asl/run/conductor on the node). A missing file or row means the documented default, a (:providerFail) row that pfErrors rejects is ignored whole and the defaults apply"
  :rung "(:rung :tier paid|strong :perDay N): caps the units that enter that rung per UTC day; no row is no cap; the lead rung is never capped but is open only while the lead heartbeat <store>/leadOnline.asn is younger than 120 s (ESC-LEAD-HOOK)"
  :providerFail "(:providerFail :backoffS S :maxInRow N :patterns (\"word\" ...)) with :patterns last, words lowercase-compared as substrings of the failed write's signature and without parentheses. A write that fails with a matching signature and no commit past its base (not stale, not vacuous) is requeued after :backoffS seconds with its fail count, signature and lane unchanged, one (:providerFail :unit :route :backoffS :n :at) row is journalled and the newest (:pw :unit :n :until) row of <store>/providerWait.asn holds the wait; the :maxInRow+1th consecutive provider failure is an ordinary failure (counted, ladder hop), any other outcome resets the run"
  :ranges "backoffS 1..3600 (default 60, adopted), maxInRow 1..100 (default 6, adopted), patterns non-empty (default err_vendor err_no_upstream \"bad gateway\" \"service unavailable\" overloaded \" 502\" \" 503\" \" 504\" \" 429\" breaker, adopted); unknown keys and out-of-range values are errors"
  :writers "(:writers :minFreeMb N :warmFirst true|false :jobserver \"DIR\" :meminfo \"PATH\") (COND-ADMIT-TOKENS): a ready unit starts its writer only while the node has a free jobserver token (tokenCount minus heldCount) and MemAvailable >= :minFreeMb; with :warmFirst (default true) the first writer after each conductor start goes alone and the rest wait until its session journal shows a served model turn, its unit left writing, or 900 s passed, recorded in <store>/warm.asn. No row, or a row with an unknown key or :minFreeMb outside 0..1000000, means no gate (checked by wrErrors, tested in conductorTest testAdmitGate). :jobserver and :meminfo default to the node's own ~/.asl/run/jobserver and /proc/meminfo and exist for tests"
  :writersRanges "minFreeMb 0..1000000 (default 2000, adopted); warmFirst default true (adopted); the node ships the row in <store>/ladder.asn, the code default without a row is no gate"
  :origin "COND-PROVIDER-FAIL-NO-HOP: 73 of 313 Leon sessions in 12 h on node2 ended ERR_VENDOR (all-breaker, rate limit) and each climbed the ladder as a writer failure")
